    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d193">

                <pb facs="0262" n="252" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg252"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.20 Mission/2–2148: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Mukden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Ward</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mukden</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-02-21T16:00:00+08:00">February 21, 1948—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 24—3:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>91. Wei Li-huang<anchor n="40" xml:id="d193-f1"/> requested me make inquiry re
                    availability “two or three” American military advisors assist him training
                    northeastern troops (Contel 121 to Embassy, 89 to Dept. February 20).<anchor
                        n="41" xml:id="d193-f2"/></p>
                <p>Sent Embassy as 125, repeated Dept as 91.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ward</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d193-f1" n="40" xml:id="d193-f1-content">
                <p>Acting Director of Generalissimo Chiang Kai-shek’s Northeast Headquarters (PNEH)
                    and Commander-in-Chief of Northeast Bandit Suppression Headquarters (NEBSH).</p>
            </note>
